Subject: [PATCH] psu: retain asserted events when hardware reads fail

Reaching the read error threshold must not synthesize a zero reading. That
would clear an existing source and, if it was the last source in its group,
publish a recovery and mark the PSU functional without hardware evidence.
Keep the last valid value and group assertions while the read is unknown;
a subsequent valid zero can clear them through the normal grouped path.

Require parsing to consume the entire value, allowing the normal sysfs
newline. A malformed value such as "0garbage" must not become a recovery.
Read/parse errors still cancel an unconfirmed predictive warning, and the
existing explicit power-state eligibility policy is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/psu/PSUEvent.cpp
+++ b/src/psu/PSUEvent.cpp
@@ -238,10 +238,16 @@
     else
     {
         const char* bufferEnd = buffer.data() + bytesTransferred;
+        // sysfs attributes end in a newline. Reject any other trailing data
+        // rather than accepting a numeric prefix as a valid clear reading.
+        if (bufferEnd != buffer.data() && bufferEnd[-1] == '\n')
+        {
+            --bufferEnd;
+        }
         int nvalue = 0;
         std::from_chars_result ret =
             std::from_chars(buffer.data(), bufferEnd, nvalue);
-        if (ret.ec != std::errc())
+        if (ret.ec != std::errc() || ret.ptr != bufferEnd)
         {
             predictionSince.reset();
             errCount++;
@@ -258,7 +264,9 @@
         {
             lg2::error("Failure to read event at '{PATH}'", "PATH", path);
         }
-        updateValue(0);
+        // A failed read does not confirm recovery. Keep the last valid value
+        // and all group assertions until a successful poll clears them.
+        // Pending predictive warnings were cancelled by the error paths.
         errCount++;
     }
     restartRead();
